  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "The diff meets both acceptance criteria. test_file_paths skips '::'-suffixed .py ids, globs, directories and tests-green.sh, and missing_test_files treats changed=None as an existence-only check. daemon.gate holds with gate_red, the 'test file not in task diff' failure lines and resume_hint.missing_test_files. changed_paths returns a list or None, which matches the isinstance(list) check in missing_test_files. I did not run the tests. The remaining issues are minor and non-blocking.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/acceptance.py",
        "line": 40,
        "issue": "Acceptance tokens are joined onto the worktree root without a containment check. An absolute path or a '..' path in a token makes is_file() probe outside the worktree. Impact is limited to an existence check on a path inside a test dir or with a test-like name, and the acceptance text is task-author data. Consider rejecting absolute and '..' tokens.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/daemon.py",
        "line": 1438,
        "issue": "The diff check is a hard hold. If acceptance names an existing test file the task legitimately did not touch (for example 'tests/foo.test.ts still passes'), the gate holds gate_red. Fix rounds that only restate acceptance are exposed to the same hold. If changed_paths returns None, the check quietly falls back to existence only.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
